WEBVTT

00:00.285 --> 00:02.352
- [Voiceover] "Vivek and Camila's
teacher gave them a system

00:02.352 --> 00:04.185
"of linear equations to solve.

00:04.185 --> 00:06.118
"They each took a few steps that lead

00:06.118 --> 00:08.284
"to the systems shown in the table below."

00:08.284 --> 00:10.052
So we have the teacher's original system,

00:10.052 --> 00:12.450
what Vivek got after
doing some operations,

00:12.450 --> 00:14.552
what Camila got after
doing some operations.

00:14.552 --> 00:17.484
Which of them obtained a
system that is equivalent

00:17.484 --> 00:19.018
to the teacher's system?

00:19.018 --> 00:20.651
So the first question
we should ask ourselves

00:20.651 --> 00:24.151
is what does it mean to even
have an equivalent system?

00:24.151 --> 00:26.152
For the sake of this
question, or for our purposes,

00:26.152 --> 00:29.918
an equivalent system is a system
that has the same solution.

00:29.918 --> 00:32.418
So if there's some X-Y pair that satisfies

00:32.418 --> 00:34.585
the teacher's system that is the solution

00:34.585 --> 00:36.218
to the teacher's system.

00:36.218 --> 00:38.418
Well Vivek's system, we're
gonna call it equivalent

00:38.418 --> 00:41.011
if it has the same solution.

00:41.011 --> 00:45.118
Similarly, if Camila's
system has the same solution,

00:45.118 --> 00:48.851
then we're gonna call it
equivalent to the teacher's system.

00:48.851 --> 00:50.751
So let's make some comparisons here.

00:50.751 --> 00:52.451
So first let's look at Vivek.

00:52.451 --> 00:55.051
So his first equation
is actually unchanged

00:55.051 --> 00:56.917
from the teacher's equation,

00:56.917 --> 00:58.618
is unchanged from the teacher's equation,

00:58.618 --> 01:02.551
so any solution that meets
both of these equations

01:02.551 --> 01:05.018
is for sure gonna meet this top equation

01:05.018 --> 01:07.251
because it's literally the
same as the top equation

01:07.251 --> 01:08.984
of the teacher, so that works out.

01:08.984 --> 01:10.521
Also look at the second one.

01:12.931 --> 01:15.551
The second one is definitely a
different equation over here.

01:15.551 --> 01:17.551
We can check that it's
not just being multiplied

01:17.551 --> 01:19.977
by some number on both sides.

01:19.977 --> 01:22.618
To go from one to zero
if you were multiplying,

01:22.618 --> 01:25.251
you would have to multiply one times zero

01:25.251 --> 01:27.351
and then in order to
maintain the equality,

01:27.351 --> 01:28.918
you would have to do that on both sides.

01:28.918 --> 01:31.218
But zero times this left-hand
side would have been zero,

01:31.218 --> 01:33.085
you would have gotten zero equals zero,

01:33.085 --> 01:36.918
so he didn't just scale
both sides by some number,

01:36.918 --> 01:38.317
looks like he did another operation.

01:38.317 --> 01:41.984
He probably looks like
he's adding or subtracting

01:41.984 --> 01:43.252
something to both sides, so let's see how

01:43.252 --> 01:45.351
he could have gotten this right over here.

01:45.351 --> 01:48.521
So he took -4x

01:48.521 --> 01:51.701
plus 5y is equal to one.

01:51.701 --> 01:53.717
And it looks like from
that he was able to get

01:53.717 --> 01:57.118
- 3x plus 7y

01:57.118 --> 01:59.288
is equal to zero.

01:59.288 --> 02:02.251
So let's see what he had to do to do that.

02:02.251 --> 02:04.818
Let's see, he would have had to,

02:04.818 --> 02:07.217
to go from -4x to -3x,

02:07.217 --> 02:09.717
he would have had to add an X,

02:09.717 --> 02:11.384
so I could just write
an X right over there.

02:11.384 --> 02:12.851
To go from 5y to 7y,

02:12.851 --> 02:14.917
he would have had to add 2y.

02:14.917 --> 02:16.717
So on the left-hand side,
he would have to add

02:16.717 --> 02:18.284
X plus 2y.

02:18.284 --> 02:20.818
Notice we have an X plus
2y right over there.

02:20.818 --> 02:23.251
And on the right-hand side,
he would have had to add

02:23.251 --> 02:25.551
or subtract a one, or add a negative one.

02:25.551 --> 02:28.251
Notice we see a negative
one right over there.

02:28.251 --> 02:32.084
So what he essentially did is
he added the left-hand sides

02:32.084 --> 02:35.451
of these two equations to
get this new left-hand side

02:35.451 --> 02:38.184
right over here, and he
added the right-hand sides

02:38.184 --> 02:39.818
to get this new right-hand side.

02:39.818 --> 02:42.534
And that is a legitimate operation.

02:42.534 --> 02:44.384
This new equation that you got,

02:44.384 --> 02:48.452
this new linear equation,
it's going to represent

02:48.452 --> 02:51.285
a different line than
this one right over here,

02:51.285 --> 02:55.018
but the resulting system is
going to have the same solution.

02:55.018 --> 02:56.984
Why do we feel confident
that the resulting system

02:56.984 --> 02:59.019
is going to have the same solution?

02:59.019 --> 03:04.019
Well for an X-Y pair that
satisfies both of these equations,

03:04.218 --> 03:06.351
that's what a solution would be,

03:06.351 --> 03:09.452
for that X-Y pair, X plus 2y

03:09.452 --> 03:11.585
is equal to negative one.

03:11.585 --> 03:13.051
So for that solution,

03:13.051 --> 03:15.385
we're adding the same thing to both sides.

03:15.385 --> 03:17.784
We're saying: "Look,
I'm gonna add X plus 2y

03:17.784 --> 03:19.884
"to the left-hand side.

03:19.884 --> 03:23.584
"Well if I don't wanna
change the solution,

03:23.584 --> 03:26.284
"I have to add the same thing
to the right-hand side."

03:26.284 --> 03:29.251
Well they're telling us for
the solution to this equation,

03:29.251 --> 03:31.584
X plus 2y is equal to negative one,

03:31.584 --> 03:34.318
so negative one is the
same thing as X plus 2y

03:34.318 --> 03:36.917
for that solution, so
we're not gonna change

03:36.917 --> 03:38.584
the resulting solution of the system,

03:38.584 --> 03:41.251
so it's a completely legitimate
operation what Vivek did

03:41.251 --> 03:42.517
is adding the left-hand sides

03:42.517 --> 03:43.751
and adding the right-hand sides

03:43.751 --> 03:45.651
to get this new second equation.

03:45.651 --> 03:47.850
That's not going to change
the solution of the system.

03:47.850 --> 03:49.518
In fact, that's a technique we often use

03:49.518 --> 03:52.185
to eventually find the
solution of a system.

03:52.185 --> 03:54.785
So now let's look at Camila, or Camila.

03:54.785 --> 03:58.318
So her first equation is
actually the exact same equation

03:58.318 --> 04:02.617
as the teacher's second equation.

04:02.617 --> 04:05.318
Now let's see, her second equation,

04:05.318 --> 04:08.351
how does it relate possibly
to the first equation?

04:08.351 --> 04:10.317
So just looking at it offhand,

04:10.317 --> 04:11.819
it looks like it might just be,

04:11.819 --> 04:14.750
it looks like she just multiplied
both sides times a number.

04:14.750 --> 04:17.485
And it looks like that
number, she clearly multiplied

04:17.485 --> 04:20.917
the right-hand side times negative eight.

04:20.917 --> 04:23.151
So times negative eight.

04:23.151 --> 04:26.884
Negative one times negative
eight is positive eight.

04:26.884 --> 04:29.051
And it looks like she also multiplied

04:29.051 --> 04:30.618
the left-hand side by negative eight.

04:30.618 --> 04:33.384
Negative eight times X is -8X.

04:33.384 --> 04:36.717
Negative eight times 2y is -16y.

04:36.717 --> 04:39.718
So she just multiplied both
sides by the same value

04:39.718 --> 04:41.284
which actually doesn't
change the equation.

04:41.284 --> 04:43.105
This actually is going to be--

04:43.105 --> 04:44.834
It changes it the way it looks,

04:44.834 --> 04:47.951
but it actually represents the same line.

04:47.951 --> 04:51.232
So this is definitely
still an equivalent system.

04:51.232 --> 04:52.851
These are still the same constraints.

04:52.851 --> 04:54.718
You're going to have the same solution.

04:54.718 --> 04:56.118
Whenever you're dealing with systems,

04:56.118 --> 04:58.818
you're not going to change
the solution of the system

04:58.818 --> 05:02.885
as long as you either multiply
both sides of an equation by

05:02.885 --> 05:05.651
a scaler, or you are adding
and subtracting the equations.

05:05.651 --> 05:07.184
When I say add or subtract the equations,

05:07.184 --> 05:09.085
you're adding the left-hand
side to the left-hand side,

05:09.085 --> 05:10.752
adding the right-hand side
to the right-hand side

05:10.752 --> 05:14.285
like we had here, or subtracting
the one from the other

05:14.285 --> 05:16.651
on the left-hand side and
if we subtract the bottom

05:16.651 --> 05:17.718
from the top on the left-hand

05:17.718 --> 05:19.751
and we subtract the bottom
from the top on the right-hand,

05:19.751 --> 05:21.785
it's not going to change our solution.

05:21.785 --> 05:25.417
So both of them obtained a
system that is equivalent,

05:25.417 --> 05:27.385
meaning that it has the same solution

05:27.385 --> 05:30.189
as the teacher's system.
